# Writing Rules (voice & tone)

Use these when writing page copy, README, or docs in this repo. Goal: clear, human, specific — not marketing-robot.

## Banned words / phrases (delete on sight)
- "mission-critical"
- "seamless"
- "performant" (prefer "fast" / "efficient")
- "robust" (prefer a concrete description of what it does)
- "cutting-edge"
- "leverage" (as a verb for "use")
- "utilize" (prefer "use")
- "game-changing" / "revolutionary"
- "effortless"
- "best-in-class"

## Banned LLM writing patterns
- "It's not just X, it's Y" constructions
- Opening with "In today's fast-paced world…"
- "Whether you're a beginner or an expert…"
- Stacking three emoji or more in a row
- Closing every paragraph with a rhetorical question
- "Unleash the power of…"

## Preferred style
- Lead with the specific claim, then the supporting detail.
- Use the second person ("you") when addressing the reader.
- One idea per sentence. Short sentences read better on a portfolio.
- Show, don't tell: name the actual tech (local-first, model-routing) instead of vague adjectives.
